From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32, localspl, winspool: makers' own print processors print EMF jobs

Canon's, HP's, Lexmark's and Ricoh's packages carry print processors of
their own (hpcpp160, LMUD1O4C, E422PP64...). Given an EMF job, such a
processor plays its pages itself through GDI's documented print processor
functions; ours were stubs and the jobs printed nothing. Now:

- gdi32: GdiGetPageCount, GdiGetPageHandle, GdiGetDC, GdiStartDocEMF,
  GdiStartPageEMF, GdiPlayPageEMF, GdiEndPageEMF, GdiEndDocEMF and
  GdiResetDCEMF, on the spool file handle GdiGetSpoolFileHandle gives (it
  kept no pages, and closed the spool file at its end). The printer is
  the job's even when the processor names the port it was opened with.
  A DC of a printer asks for the newest EMF datatype its print processor
  takes (makers' take "NT EMF 1.008" only; we always asked for 1.003).
- localspl: what a processor draws on its printer's DC while it prints a
  job is not a new job: it is printed by winprint through the driver to
  the job's port; raw data it writes goes to the port.
- winspool: EnumPrintProcessorDatatypes asks the print processor (it was
  a stub).

HP's, Lexmark's and Ricoh's print processors now print their printers'
jobs (PCL XL, PCL 5, PostScript).

Test: test/printproc-gate.sh with test/printproc-fixture.c, a print
processor of our own (mutants SG_MUTANT_PLAYPAGE, EMFTYPE, SPOOLPRINTER,
PPDATATYPES, DIRECTJOB).
